  "configuration_id": "config_026",
  "reason": "We have two data points: RNA-only (pca_n2000, singleprofile) at 0.4849 acc and multimodal (pca_n2000 + resnet50, concat, singleprofile) at 0.5266 acc. The ~4.2% gap suggests image information helps, but we cannot yet decompose whether the gain comes from the image signal itself, the fusion mechanism, or architectural complexity. config_026 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the exact image-only counterpart to config_045, completing the RNA-only / image-only / multimodal decomposition with all other settings held constant. If image-only is near 0.48, the multimodal gain is primarily from RNA; if near 0.53, image dominates; if in between, both modalities contribute additively. This decomposition is the single most important piece of missing evidence: it determines whether future budget should target better image encoders, better RNA encoders, better fusion strategies, or multiprofile aggregation. No other available configuration isolates this question as cleanly with a single variable change from an already-tested setting."
}

